# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# H-33  VARIABLE WING AREA MORPHING — STOW / SWEEP / POWER SPECTRUM
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# CONCEPT (corrected and complete):
#
#   The MCO-1D can place any wing pair into one of three distinct aerodynamic
#   states, independently of every other pair, at any time during flight.
#
#   STATE A — ACTIVE FLAPPING (normal):
#     Sector oscillating at commanded amplitude and frequency.
#     Generates lift via unsteady aerodynamics + LEV augmentation + thrust.
#     All four pairs in State A = maximum lift, minimum wing loading,
#     maximum gust sensitivity.
#
#   STATE B — STOPPED AT NEUTRAL (fixed-wing glide / partial tuck):
#     Amplitude commanded to zero.  Wing held stationary at mid-stroke,
#     approximately horizontal at operating AoA.
#     At forward speed V the stopped wing generates lift exactly as a fixed
#     wing: L = ½ρV²S·CL(α).  At V=7 m/s with S1223 at 8° AoA (CL≈1.2)
#     a W1 pair contributes ~8.8 N — about 26% of MTOW.
#     NO thrust is generated.  Unsteady augmentation is lost.
#     The stopped pair does NOT drop out of the lift budget — it demotes
#     from active+unsteady to passive+fixed.  Active pairs compensate only
#     for the DIFFERENCE between flapping-lift and fixed-wing-lift,
#     not the full missing lift.
#     Gust response of the stopped pair is gentler than a flapping pair
#     because it has no AoA excursions — it responds as a passive aerofoil.
#
#   STATE C — STOWED ALONG FUSELAGE (full tuck):
#     Sweep servo commanded to maximum-aft position (~80-90° from neutral).
#     Wing lies approximately parallel to fuselage axis.
#     Planform area presented to flow → near zero.
#     AoA relative to airstream → near zero.
#     Lift contribution → negligible.
#     Gust loading on stowed pair → negligible (nothing for the gust to act on).
#     Active pairs must compensate the FULL missing lift.
#     Wing loading on active surface rises sharply.
#     Gust sensitivity falls sharply on the active surface per the formula:
#       Δn = ρ·V·Ude·a / (2·W/S)
#     where W/S is now computed over active wing area only.
#
#   CRITICAL INSIGHT — SWEEP TRIM COMPENSATION:
#     When any pair is stowed, the centre of lift shifts.
#     The ACTIVE pairs' sweep servos absorb this entirely.
#     Sweeping an active pair forward moves its lift centroid forward.
#     Sweeping it aft moves the centroid aft.
#     The optimizer controls sweep continuously across all active pairs.
#     Therefore ANY pair can be stowed without a fixed pitch trim penalty —
#     the active pairs re-trim themselves through sweep.
#     This eliminates the CG/pitch constraint I incorrectly cited before.
#
#   POWER VARIANTS (the third dimension):
#     A stopped pair (State B) consumes zero motor power.
#     A stowed pair (State C) consumes zero motor power.
#     The freed motor power budget can be redistributed to active pairs,
#     allowing them to run at higher frequency than the 4-pair hover point.
#     This directly enables higher forward speed:
#       - Fewer active pairs → higher wing loading → higher cruise speed
#         before gust sensitivity becomes unacceptable
#       - Freed power to active pairs → more thrust → higher speed
#       - Fixed-wing contribution of State B pairs at cruise speed
#         may partially offset the missing flapping lift
#       - Net result: a speed regime where fewer-pair configurations
#         outperform the 4-pair configuration
#
#   BIOLOGICAL GROUNDING:
#     Swift (Lentink et al. Nature 2007):
#       "Extended wings superior for slow glides; swept wings superior for
#        fast glides and turns."
#       Choosing optimal sweep halves sink speed or triples turning rate.
#       State B (stopped neutral) ≈ extended glide.
#       State C (fuselage stow) ≈ full-sweep fast configuration.
#
#     Steppe eagle (Reynolds et al. J. Royal Soc. Interface 2014):
#       Wing tucks occur more frequently under higher atmospheric turbulence.
#       Tuck = transient State B→C transition as active gust alleviation.
#       MCO-1D can sustain this state deliberately, not just transiently.
#
#     Peregrine falcon in stoop:
#       Wings in M-shape (near State C) at 240+ mph.
#       Near-zero effective wing area = near-zero gust Δn.
#       Maximum penetration speed with minimal gust disturbance.
#
#   QUANTIFIED WING LOADING PER CONFIGURATION (at MTOW 3.448 kg):
#     4 pairs active:            W/S_active = 3.52 kg/m²  (baseline)
#     3 pairs active + 1 stowed: W/S_active = 4.70 kg/m²  (+34%)
#     2 pairs active + 2 stowed: W/S_active = 7.04 kg/m²  (+100%)
#     1 pair  active + 3 stowed: W/S_active = 13.5 kg/m²  (+284%)
#     Note: State B (stopped neutral) contributes fixed-wing lift so the
#     active pairs carry less than the full MTOW in practice.
#
#   VARIANTS REGISTERED (18 total):
#     v01  W1 stowed (State C), W2/3/4 active — front pair tucked
#     v02  W4 stowed (State C), W1/2/3 active — rear pair tucked
#     v03  W2 stowed (State C), W1/3/4 active — second pair tucked
#     v04  W3 stowed (State C), W1/2/4 active — third pair tucked
#     v05  W1+W4 stowed, W2+W3 active — ends stowed, middles active
#     v06  W2+W3 stowed, W1+W4 active — middles stowed, ends active
#     v07  W1+W2 stowed, W3+W4 active — front half stowed
#     v08  W3+W4 stowed, W1+W2 active — rear half stowed
#     v09  W1 stopped at neutral (State B), W2/3/4 active — partial tuck
#     v10  W4 stopped at neutral (State B), W1/2/3 active — partial tuck
#     v11  W1+W4 stopped (State B), W2+W3 active — ends neutral
#     v12  W1 stowed + max power to W2/3/4 — speed-biased front tuck
#     v13  W4 stowed + max power to W1/2/3 — speed-biased rear tuck
#     v14  W1+W4 stowed + max power to W2+W3 — speed-biased end tuck
#     v15  W2+W3 stowed + max power to W1+W4 — speed-biased mid tuck
#     v16  Speed-adaptive: auto-stow W4 when V > 6 m/s
#     v17  Speed-adaptive: auto-stow W1+W4 when V > 9 m/s
#     v18  Gust-adaptive: auto-stow nearest pair when sigma_roll > 5°
#
#   SCORED ON:
#     PRIMARY:  gust rejection (sigma_h, sigma_roll at cruise speed)
#     SECONDARY: cruise speed achieved (V_ms = pitot airspeed from Pixhawk)
#     TERTIARY:  power efficiency (bus current vs altitude hold quality)
#     The discovery focus mode 'morphing_speed' weights these appropriately.
#
#   GATED ON TC-03:
#     All stowed-pair variants require the CT-J curve from TC-03 to know
#     whether the remaining active pairs can sustain level flight at the
#     target speed.  State B variants (stopped neutral) are safe to attempt
#     in TC-04 because the stopped pair still contributes fixed-wing lift.
#     State C variants (full stow) require TC-03 confirmation first.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Wing area constants (derived from SEMI_SPANS_MM and CHORD_MM) ──────────

_H33_CHORD_M     = CHORD_MM / 1000.0
_H33_PAIR_AREA   = {
    1: 2 * (SEMI_SPANS_MM[1] / 1000.0) * _H33_CHORD_M,   # W1 pair m²
    2: 2 * (SEMI_SPANS_MM[2] / 1000.0) * _H33_CHORD_M,   # W2 pair m²
    3: 2 * (SEMI_SPANS_MM[3] / 1000.0) * _H33_CHORD_M,   # W3 pair m²
    4: 2 * (SEMI_SPANS_MM[4] / 1000.0) * _H33_CHORD_M,   # W4 pair m²
}
_H33_S_TOTAL     = sum(_H33_PAIR_AREA.values())   # ~0.9794 m²

# Approximate fixed-wing CL for State B (stopped neutral, best-glide AoA ~8°)
# S1223 at Re 50k, 8° AoA → CL ≈ 1.2
_H33_CL_NEUTRAL  = 1.2

# Sweep position definitions
_H33_SWEEP_NEUTRAL_DEG = 60.0    # mid-range neutral position
_H33_SWEEP_STOW_DEG    = 95.0    # near-fuselage stow (max aft available)
_H33_SWEEP_FWD_DEG     = 30.0    # full forward for trim compensation


def _h33_wing_loading(active_pairs, V_ms, rho=1.225):
    """
    Compute effective wing loading and fixed-wing lift contribution
    for a given set of active pairs and forward speed.

    active_pairs : list of pair indices (1-4) that are flapping
    V_ms         : forward airspeed

    Returns dict with:
      S_active_m2      : area of actively flapping wings
      W_S_active       : wing loading on active surface (kg/m²)
      L_fixed_N        : lift from State B stopped pairs (at neutral)
      L_needed_N       : lift active pairs must generate
      delta_n_factor   : relative gust sensitivity vs 4-pair baseline
    """
    S_active  = sum(_H33_PAIR_AREA[p] for p in active_pairs)
    # Fixed-wing lift from stopped (State B) pairs at forward speed
    # Only pairs that are stopped at neutral (not stowed) contribute
    L_fixed   = 0.5 * rho * V_ms**2 * _H33_CL_NEUTRAL * (
                    _H33_S_TOTAL - S_active)
    L_needed  = max(0.0, MTOW_KG * 9.81 - L_fixed)
    W_S       = MTOW_KG / max(S_active, 0.01)
    # Gust Δn scales inversely with W/S on active surface
    W_S_base  = MTOW_KG / _H33_S_TOTAL
    delta_n   = W_S_base / W_S    # <1 means less gust sensitivity
    return {
        'S_active_m2':    round(S_active, 4),
        'W_S_active':     round(W_S, 2),
        'L_fixed_N':      round(L_fixed, 2),
        'L_needed_N':     round(L_needed, 2),
        'delta_n_factor': round(delta_n, 3),
    }


def _h33_make_config(
        stowed_pairs,         # list of pair indices to stow (State C)
        stopped_pairs,        # list of pair indices to stop at neutral (State B)
        power_boost,          # float: multiply active pair freq by this factor
        speed_adaptive_v,     # float or None: V_ms at which to trigger
        gust_adaptive,        # bool: auto-trigger on sigma_roll
        variant_label,        # str: variant identifier
        base_config=None):
    """
    Build a complete H-33 configuration dict for one variant.

    The optimizer receives this config and maps it to per-wing commands:
      - stowed pairs:  amplitude=0, sweep=STOW, motor idle
      - stopped pairs: amplitude=0, sweep=NEUTRAL, AoA=best-glide
      - active pairs:  normal flapping with sweep adjusted for trim,
                       frequency scaled by power_boost
    """
    cfg = dict(base_config or {})

    all_pairs   = {1, 2, 3, 4}
    stowed_s    = set(stowed_pairs)
    stopped_s   = set(stopped_pairs)
    active_s    = all_pairs - stowed_s - stopped_s

    cfg['h33_stowed_pairs']        = sorted(stowed_s)
    cfg['h33_stopped_pairs']       = sorted(stopped_s)
    cfg['h33_active_pairs']        = sorted(active_s)
    cfg['h33_power_boost']         = round(power_boost, 3)
    cfg['h33_speed_adaptive_v']    = speed_adaptive_v
    cfg['h33_gust_adaptive']       = gust_adaptive
    cfg['h33_variant']             = variant_label

    # Per-wing command overrides
    wing_cmds = {}
    for pair in sorted(stowed_s):
        for side in ('p', 's'):
            wing_cmds[f'W{pair}{side}'] = {
                'state':        'stowed',
                'amplitude':    0.0,
                'sweep_deg':    _H33_SWEEP_STOW_DEG,
                'aoa_deg':      0.0,    # flat to airstream
                'motor':        'idle',
            }
    for pair in sorted(stopped_s):
        for side in ('p', 's'):
            wing_cmds[f'W{pair}{side}'] = {
                'state':        'stopped_neutral',
                'amplitude':    0.0,
                'sweep_deg':    _H33_SWEEP_NEUTRAL_DEG,
                'aoa_deg':      AOA_BEST_LD_DEG_RE50K,   # best-glide AoA
                'motor':        'idle',
            }
    # Active pairs get sweep trim compensation
    # Distribute sweep across active pairs to maintain pitch trim
    # Pairs forward of CG: sweep aft to compensate forward-shifted lift
    # Pairs aft of CG: sweep forward to compensate aft-shifted lift
    # Simple heuristic: if stowed pairs have lower index (front), sweep
    # active pairs forward; if higher index (rear), sweep aft.
    if stowed_s or stopped_s:
        stowed_indices = sorted(stowed_s | stopped_s)
        mean_stowed    = sum(stowed_indices) / len(stowed_indices) if stowed_indices else 2.5
        # If stowed pairs are in front (low index), active pairs compensate
        # by sweeping forward to move their lift centroid forward.
        if mean_stowed < 2.5:
            active_sweep = _H33_SWEEP_FWD_DEG + 10.0   # forward of neutral
        elif mean_stowed > 2.5:
            active_sweep = _H33_SWEEP_NEUTRAL_DEG + 15.0  # aft of neutral
        else:
            active_sweep = _H33_SWEEP_NEUTRAL_DEG   # balanced
    else:
        active_sweep = _H33_SWEEP_NEUTRAL_DEG

    for pair in sorted(active_s):
        for side in ('p', 's'):
            wing_cmds[f'W{pair}{side}'] = {
                'state':         'active',
                'freq_boost':    power_boost,
                'sweep_deg':     round(active_sweep, 1),
                'motor':         'active',
                # AoA and amplitude are optimizer-controlled
            }

    cfg['h33_wing_cmds']    = wing_cmds
    cfg['h33_n_active']     = len(active_s)
    cfg['h33_n_stowed']     = len(stowed_s)
    cfg['h33_n_stopped']    = len(stopped_s)

    # Pre-compute loading metrics at representative cruise speed
    metrics = _h33_wing_loading(sorted(active_s), V_ms=7.0)
    cfg['h33_metrics_7ms']  = metrics

    cfg['hypothesis']   = 'H-33'
    cfg['bio_source']   = 'variable_wing_area_morphing_stow_sweep_power'
    cfg['reference']    = ('Swift wing morphing (Lentink et al. Nature 2007); '
                           'Steppe eagle wing tuck (Reynolds et al. JRSI 2014); '
                           'Peregrine stoop morphology (Gowree et al. CommsBio 2018)')
    cfg['tc_gate']      = ('State B variants safe for TC-04. '
                           'State C variants require TC-03 CT-J curve first.')
    return cfg


