#            within 1.5s, without overshoot. Front side of power curve.
#
#   H-PF-2: Back-side pilot feel — as speed reduces below best L/D,
#            pitch controls airspeed and power controls altitude.
#            The feel inverts; the pilot must sense this naturally.
#
#   H-PF-3: Nose attitude continuity through blend zone — fuselage pitch
#            attitude changes no more than 3°/s through 3-5 m/s.
#            The aircraft does NOT pitch up dramatically at transition speed.
#
#   H-PF-4: Hover departure nose management — as the aircraft accelerates
#            from hover into forward flight, the nose attitude evolves
#            naturally from level-body hover through slight pitch-up at the
#            back-side regime into level cruise attitude.
#            The reverse of H-PF-3; same smoothness criterion.
