# H-FD-4: NEAR-VERTICAL DIHEDRAL — MAXIMUM DRAG BRAKE
#
# The unexplored regime: 70-85° dihedral.
# At 80°, wing tips are 0.76m above the mounting point and only 0.13m
# from the fuselage centreline. The wings are nearly vertical.
# Lift approaches zero. Drag approaches maximum.
# This is a pure aerodynamic brake — the ornithopter equivalent of
# a parachute or a plane's speedbrake deployed to near-90°.
#
# The pigeon does use this range during very steep final approach onto
# a narrow perch — the near-vertical wing configuration in the last
# 0.5-1.0 seconds produces maximum deceleration without any body pitch.
#
# For the MCO-1D: lever 0% maps to this configuration at the extreme.
# It is the maximum of the pigeon steep descent zone.
